A directory, a directory with a trailing slash, and a glob give one glob view of all their files in path order; a Markdown file without frontmatter prints its first heading.
== args
input/src
input/docs/
input/config/*.md
== file input/src/utils.md
---
description: Utility functions.
---
# utils
== file input/src/helpers/nested.md
---
description: Helper functions.
---
# helpers
== file input/docs/readme.md
---
title: Documentation
---
== file input/docs/guide.md
# User Guide
== file input/config/settings.md
---
description: Config settings.
---
# settings
== stdout
glob view: input/src input/docs/ input/config/*.md
input/config/settings.md (4 lines): description: "Config settings."
input/docs/guide.md (1 line): # User Guide
input/docs/readme.md (3 lines): title: "Documentation"
input/src/helpers/nested.md (4 lines): description: "Helper functions."
input/src/utils.md (4 lines): description: "Utility functions."
